A lot of weak monsters (orcs and so on) are generated carrying
them.  If you're deadly enough to frequently send them to their
grave in one hit, you collect a lot of teleport scrolls.  Personally
I usually blank most of them, but if you don't, and you don't
leave them laying around on the floor, you could easily end up
with 60+ of the things.

> > The Astral was not really that bad either, despite not realizing I had
> > forgotten my helm of opposite alignment in the dungeons and as a
> > result ending up going to all 3 altars till I found mine.

In my experience, everything on the astral plane is rather
seriously underpowered compared to the Wizard of Yendor.
It's anticlimactic, if Rodney doesn't show up on Astral.

The first time I got to the astral plane, I intended to do a
comparison of the riders, to see whether I agree with the
conventional wisdom as to which one is the "big threat".
I went to all three altars and killed all three of the riders
at least twice each, but I was unable to discern any real
difference between them in terms of difficulty.  I'd have
stuck around longer and played with them some more
(they weren't scaring me at all), but Rodney would have
showed up eventually, and I *was* a little afraid of him,
so I went ahead and finished up at that point.

